.TH CYAML_DOUBLE_VAL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_double_val \- extract a floating-point value from a CYAML_FLOAT node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

double cyaml_double_val(cyaml node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Return the double that node stores.  The function calls ccol_fatal_err()
when node is NULL, and it calls ccol_fatal_err() as well when node is not
of type CYAML_FLOAT.  The returned value can be infinite or NaN (see
cyaml_create_double_mp).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
node  CYAML_FLOAT node.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The double value.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_type (3),
.BR cyaml_create_double (3)
